var NO_AGE_GATE_EXCERPT = " NO AGE GATE VARIANT (us.federal.eitc_no_age_gate): recomputes this SAME \xA7 32(a)-(b), (f), (i) credit with the \xA7 32(c)(1)(A)(ii) childless-filer age requirement (25-64) removed entirely \u2014 i.e. the isAge65OrOlder/isAtLeastAge25 facts are never consulted, so a childless filer of ANY age reaches the ordinary table/formula math. Exists solely to feed STATE statutes that expressly decouple from the federal age floor, e.g. Illinois (35 ILCS 5/212(b-5) for 18-24, (b-10) for 65+, P.A. 102-700: 'based on the federal tax credit for which the taxpayer would have been eligible without regard to any age requirements... in Section 32(c)(1)(A)(ii)'). This rule's own federal answer is NOT a valid federal EITC \u2014 it is an intermediate for us.il.eitc (and any other state with an identical decoupling statute) and must never be substituted for us.federal.eitc on the federal return itself.";
