      excerpt: "\u2026shall not exceed $12,500 ($25,000 in the case of a joint return)\u2026 reduced (but not below zero) by $100 for each $1,000 by which the taxpayer's modified adjusted gross income exceeds $150,000 ($300,000 in the case of a joint return). Qualified overtime compensation means the FLSA \xA7 7 premium in excess of the regular rate. [Married taxpayers must file jointly \u2014 MFS gets $0. SSN assumed satisfied.]"
